{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nA maintainer checking a release locally runs the command docs/releasing.md step 1 gives (`python -m build && python -m twine check dist/*`, docs/releasing.md:339-340). On a correct tree it fails, and the artifact it checks is not the one release.yml publishes, so the local check can neither pass nor predict the release.\n\n## Observation (2026-11-09, release 0.15.0 at ab534d1b382; reproduced 2026-11-18 at 7e442645e51)\n- In a `make worktree` venv, `python -m twine` fails: No module named twine. twine is only in .github/release-requirements.txt.\n- `python -m build` (isolated) resolves pyproject's `hatchling>=1.27` (pyproject.toml:2) to the newest hatchling and produces a wheel and sdist with Metadata-Version 2.5. The release-pinned twine 6.2.0 rejects both: \"InvalidDistribution: Invalid distribution metadata: '2.5' is not a valid metadata version\".\n- Root cause of the rejection is twine, not packaging: the locked packaging 26.2 lists '2.5' in `packaging.metadata._VALID_METADATA_VERSIONS`, but twine 6.2.0 `twine/package.py` overwrites that list with its own hardcoded list that stops at 2.4. twine 7.0.0 (current PyPI) checks the same 2.5 artifacts as PASSED.\n- The release.yml path (fresh venv, `pip install --require-hashes --no-deps -r .github/release-requirements.txt`, hatchling 1.31.0, `python -m build --no-isolation`, release.yml:137-159) produces Metadata-Version 2.4, and twine 6.2.0 `twine check` passes both artifacts.\n\n## Approach\nGive maintainers one command that runs exactly release.yml's build-and-check path, instead of making the isolated build pass: a check that builds with a different toolchain than the release cannot predict the release, whatever twine version it uses.\n- New `scripts/release_build_check.py` (stdlib only, so it runs from any venv on any OS). It creates a fresh venv in a temporary directory with `venv.EnvBuilder(with_pip=True)` (the venv interpreter path comes from the builder context's `env_exe`, so no `bin/` vs `Scripts/` assumption), then runs release.yml's build-job steps in order with that interpreter: `pip install --require-hashes --no-deps -r .github/release-requirements.txt`; `pip freeze` captured to a file and passed to `scripts/check_build_env_locked.py --lock ... --freeze ...`; `python -m build --no-isolation --outdir <tmp>/dist`; `python -m twine check` on the wheel and sdist. It stops at the first failing step, names that step, and exits non-zero; on success it prints the artifact directory. The step list is built by a pure function (`release_build_steps`) so a unit test can compare it with release.yml.\n- New Makefile target `release-build-check` running the script (the same shape as the existing `verify-mcp-pin` target, Makefile:509-510).\n- docs/releasing.md step 1's local sanity line uses `make release-build-check`, with one sentence on why a bare `python -m build` differs (newest hatchling emits Metadata-Version 2.5, which the pinned twine 6.2.0 rejects).\ntwine is not added to the dev extra: the check installs it from the hash-locked release lock, the same version the release uses.\n\n## Scope\n- `scripts/release_build_check.py` (new).\n- `tests/unit/test_release_build_check.py` (new).\n- `Makefile` — `release-build-check` target and `.PHONY` entry.\n- `docs/releasing.md` — step 1 local sanity line.\n\n## Testing\n- `tests/unit/test_release_build_check.py`, written first:\n  - parity: every command fragment of release.yml's `build` job steps \"Build sdist + wheel\" and \"Validate metadata\" (`--require-hashes --no-deps -r .github/release-requirements.txt`, `check_build_env_locked.py`, `build --no-isolation`, `twine check`) appears in `release_build_steps()`, in the same order.\n  - failure path: with an injected runner that fails the build step, `main` returns non-zero, does not run twine, and the error names the failed step.\n  - the Makefile defines `release-build-check` and it invokes the script.\n- Live: `make release-build-check` on the change's tree passes (needs network for the pinned pip install), and its output shows Metadata-Version 2.4 artifacts with twine `PASSED`.\n- `make verify` passes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A documented local command reproduces release.yml's build and twine check, and passes on a correct tree. Checked: docs/releasing.md names `make release-build-check`, and running it on merged main exits 0 with both artifacts `PASSED`.\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/test_release_build_check.py` passes on merged main, including the release.yml parity test.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795058299470928570,"uuid":"87c094d1-c9dd-4b25-abb6-e74d17442243"}